## Compliance Acknowledgment

**Anti-Lazy Directive** — Acknowledged. Every file I emit will be complete. No `// ... rest of`, no `// TODO`, no elided function bodies, no "same as above" references. If a function is declared, it is implemented.

**Strict Memory Management** — Acknowledged. Every `BufferGeometry`, `Material`, `Texture`, `RenderTarget`, and `AudioNode` I allocate will have a traceable owner and an explicit teardown path. Every game module exposes a `dispose()` that walks its own resource ledger; pooled objects are recycled, never re-allocated; `EffectComposer` render targets are resized, not recreated.

**Sequential Output Protocol** — Acknowledged. One game at a time. `plan.md` on "Begin [Game Name]", full implementation only on "Plan approved". On truncation I resume from the exact cut character with no preamble.

